		<Item class="Script" referent="RBX34">
			<Properties>
				<bool name="Disabled">true</bool>
				<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
				<string name="Name">readme</string>
				<ProtectedString name="Source">--[[

The new lobby for the Halloween version? I&apos;m thinking it could be a classic, simple thing: in the depths of the forest.
It could have some other features too, here are some ideas:

Dirt pathway, maybe a circular design with all the things around the sides before blocking the out-of-bounds with trees and bushes and stuff?
Campfire, and logs to sit around it. (This has to be added if we&apos;re doing this setting!)
Camping tents and sleeping bags
Lanterns (although we don&apos;t have dynamic lighting, so maybe not, unless they&apos;re shut off)
Fireflies
(add more ideas if you have them)

HOW TO FIREFLIES: steal bird flying script from that one forest map from 2006-2007
HOW TO LATERN: use transparent balls

I think ambient sounds like crickets and a crackling fire (if we add the campfire) would be really cool too. 
Of course, it&apos;s just an optional thing that people can choose to download manually. (The modern Roblox version would have them uploaded to Roblox and enabled for everyone.)

potential additons:
- have an arrow point to pit for people&apos;s first play throughs (clientsided through camera)
- have a pop up if they say &quot;LOUD&quot; which tells them how to turn down volume
- figure out why the slingshot sounds like 2 are coming out when its just 1 when in server
- find another song for campsite (my speakers started squeaking)

--]]</ProtectedString>
